{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3972-beyond-refinements","id":3972,"title":"Beyond Refinements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T20:33:01-08:00","id":3972,"title":"Beyond Refinements","content":"I am beginning work on a new Promethean campaign that will be utilizing the new rules of the WoD (not yet sure how to incorporate those changes into the Promethean specific-stuff but I see some people have already been considering that). As I'm thinking about the changes to the system and considering the direction I want the campaign to go I'm wondering what Refinements would start to look like if Promethean society had a chance to become a bit more cohesive than it was. Say at any point there were about two or three dozen in a pretty wide region that regularly ran into each other - wouldn't their concepts of the Great Work become a bit more refined as they went along? And wouldn't these philosophical ideologies become quite extensive given a long enough Pilgrimage? And wouldn't these entrenched concepts get passed down to younger Prometheans?<br /> <br /> Obviously I kind of think so and I'm interested in hearing what other people think this would look like.<br /> <br /> I have this basic idea that Refinements are like general interests and areas that Prometheans are focused on but that, beyond Refinements, there are Roads (although that name shifts more towards pilgrimage metaphors and away from alchemical ones). Roads include entire mythologies and dogmas but are frequently rooted in one Refinement - though they can certainly be rooted in 2 or more or none at all.<br /> <br /> One of my interests in this is that the campaign concept I am developing so far involves the Throng being commanded by a quashmallum to record their efforts towards the New Dawn as a kind of bible / guidebook for those that will come after them..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:08:49-08:00","id":3984,"title":"","content":"Ah, prometheans going to tier 2 or 3, not what I thought you were going there.<br /> <br /> This is something I've thought about, barring any grand vision I'd use the cult rules, have the groups form around a single thing.<br /> <br /> One idea I had is for a group of prometheans forming into a collection of monster clowns, that disquiet is why people are afraid of clowns. <br /> <br /> Or perhaps a group of centimani who are trying to enhance themselves with cybertechnology after stumbling across some godmachine tech.<br /> <br /> Things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:28:27-08:00","id":4004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3972-beyond-refinements?p=3984#post3984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah, prometheans going to tier 2 or 3, not what I thought you were going there.<br /> <br /> This is something I've thought about, barring any grand vision I'd use the cult rules, have the groups form around a single thing.<br /> <br /> One idea I had is for a group of prometheans forming into a collection of monster clowns, that disquiet is why people are afraid of clowns.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps a group of centimani who are trying to enhance themselves with cybertechnology after stumbling across some godmachine tech.<br /> <br /> Things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read over the cult rules and, while I like them, I like the idea of Roads granting access to particularly esoteric Transmutations or something too. Perhaps it would be taken as a Merit and the Merit would function identically to the cult save that it would also allow them to purchase that Road's Transmutation up to the dots they have in the &quot;cult initiation&quot; merit. The drawback to this added benefit is that they are bound to a specific dogma in order for their Transmutations to function and certain social obligations to stay in the good graces of fellow Road members who might teach the Transmutation. Maybe? I don't know. Just a total spitball there.<br /> <br /> I would be terrified of all the ICP references my group would make if I introduced clowns in any manner. The Centimani who are &quot;upgrading&quot; themselves is a fascinating idea as it may be that they are hoping their Pilgrimage takes them right past the human experience to a transhuman experience...which is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:36:32-08:00","id":4011,"title":"","content":"Although I guess this concept really kind of requires examples to be fleshed out. Might be a project for tomorrow night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:56:09-08:00","id":4681,"title":"","content":"Well a group could certainly teach rare transmutations, transmutations are something someone either knows or doesn't know, barring a cult having psi cops in their ranks a promethean is always going to know a transmutation once learnt.<br /> <br /> I'd also decouple the idea of these second tier or even third tier groups being connected to the refinements, refinements are general philosophies.<br /> <br /> For example, how many communist organizations have their been? How many times have those groups come into conflict, either over ideology or practical concerns?<br /> <br /> You want a group of prometheans that has a background from a certain refinement, that's fine, but that doesn't stop a billion other possible groups that share the same refinement, or forming over things that don't have a damn thing to do with refinement. There's not a thing stopping a group being defined by lineage, wretched who study mad science, ulgans who made a deal with a specific choir of spirits. Or something else entirely, like those monster clowns, or perhaps a group of promethean sewer workers who are trying to form a promethean society underground.<br /> <br /> When the werewolf chroniclers guide hacked the setting to bring werewolf into tier three, it wasn't about making the tribes tier three, it added new organizations that were tier three.<br /> <br /> And prometheans change refinements all the time, it's part of their growth process. Any group that kicks out their members for changing refinement would be leaking members like the titanic leaked water, and these members would be taking whatever transmutations or other secrets with them, and would have no loyalty impeding them from spreading those secrets around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T23:03:48-08:00","id":15162,"title":"","content":"Okay then, so maybe a question would be what do people imagine might be the Tier 3 organizations that bind Promethean society together? I have already suggested that beyond the philosophical points of Refinements there might be religious doctrines that are less flexible. What other ideas are out there? I think it's a given that any organization that actually adds structure and consistency to the Promethean experience is in some way a really big diversion from the game as it is currently (which is not necessarily a good or bad thing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:36:17-08:00","id":15205,"title":"","content":"Ah well I was thinking more tier two with my ideas, prometheans forming cults and gangs and self help groups is tier two, for tier three the only thing I can think of is taking the refinements and turning the dial to 11.<br /> <br /> At tier three there might be the watchmen, a secret police of prometheans who protect the prometheans.<br /> <br /> Scholars who would probably act a lot like the ordo dracul, store houses of occult lore and the diplomats dealing with the other supernaturals, maybe even spies who have infiltrated the other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Chameleons who act as spies, assuming any identity as needed, covering up incidents that might expose the promethean.<br /> <br /> Transhumanists who seek to start the next step in human evolution, genetic engineering, cybernetics, memetic manipulation, builders of humanity 2.0<br /> <br /> Psychologists who seek to remove psychological issues from prometheans, perhaps trying to undo disquiet with logic and emotional intelligence.<br /> <br /> Perfectionists who use hypnosis to become better than they are and manipulate others.<br /> <br /> Assassins who eliminate threats to the prometheans.<br /> <br /> Angelologists who deal with quashmallam and study pyros .<br /> <br /> Doctors who understand prometheans inside and out, acting as medics among other things.<br /> <br /> Lunatics, masters of torment who drive men mad as social assassins.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's all I can think of offhand.<br /> <br /> But at tier three, the prometheans are manipulators of men, not fugitives hiding at the fringe, perhaps they should be even more gonzo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}